<title>BRAZIL: Hyundai briefs Cardoso on Brazil plant.</title>
<headline>Hyundai briefs Cardoso on Brazil plant.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials from South Korea's Hyundai Motor Co Ltd met Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso Thursday to explain their plan to invest $280 million in a new vehicle plant in the country, an official said.</p>
<p>Hyundai plans to build 40,000 vans and minivans at the plant in Simoes Filho, Bahia state, presidential spokesman Sergio Amaral said.</p>
<p>The plant, which would create 1,000 new jobs, was due to begin producing the vehicles from March 1999, he said.</p>
<p>Hyundai is one of several companies to take advantage of fiscal incentives offered by the Brazilian government to international carmakers setting up factories in the country's poor northeast.</p>
<p>About $1.7 billion worth of investments have so far been announced under the plan.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193))</p>
